meta {
  name: Resolve From Install
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/invite/resolve
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "referrer": "utm_source=beaconu&utm_medium=invite&ref={{studentReferralCode}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Deferred deep link resolution. The app calls this on first open with whatever
  it recovered after installation:

    referrer — raw Play Install Referrer string (Android). Parsed server-side
               so the link format can change without an app release. The code
               is read from the `ref` (or `referral_code`) param.
    code     — the code directly: a Universal/App Link opened the installed
               app, or the user typed it in manually (the iOS path, since iOS
               has no Install Referrer equivalent).

  Send at least one of the two; sending both prefers `code`.

  ALWAYS returns 200, never 404 — an organic install legitimately has no
  referral and must not look like an error. Response is
  { valid: true, code: "..." } or { valid: false, code: null }.

  Contrast with GET /public/invite/:code, which DOES 404 on an unknown code:
  that one answers "is this specific code real?", this one answers "did this
  install come from an invite, and if so which?".

  Table: student_referral_codes
}
